{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfvKb2B4UJMU4xJQJpivL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`vitest --repeats <n>` runs every test n extra times, and it does this whether the test passes or fails. That makes it useful for finding flaky tests, which only fail some of the time. It works differently from `--retry`. `--retry` only re-runs a test after it fails, so one passing run is enough to count it as a pass. With `--repeats`, every run has to succeed.\n\nWhere this comes from: the project's `.ludion/lessons.md` says the CLI flag was added in vitest 5.0.0, and you have 5.0.3 installed. The idea isn't new, though: older versions already had a per-test `repeats` option, as in `test('name', { repeats: 5 }, fn)`. I haven't run the flag in this project, so `npx vitest --help` will confirm it's there and show the exact syntax."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7620,"cache_read_input_tokens":15764,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7620},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"23b6256f-6505-4c8e-bd0b-67dbe95a103f","uuid":"3cc01e45-1c12-406c-96e6-abf65f149eea","timestamp":"2026-10-11T10:50:46.577Z","request_id":"req_011CfvKb1ugmV4u4egvf59BL"}
